          "stem": "Given \\(z=\\frac{\\sqrt3+i}{1+i}\\), find \\(z^5\\).",
          "hint": "Convert numerator and denominator to modulus-argument form before raising to the fifth power.",
          "solution": "\\(4\\sqrt2e^{19i\\pi/12}\\)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Find modulus and argument of each factor.",
              "work": "\\(\\sqrt3+i=2e^{i\\pi/6},\\quad 1+i=\\sqrt2e^{i\\pi/4}.\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Divide in polar form.",
              "work": "\\(z=\\sqrt2e^{-i\\pi/12}.\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Apply De Moivre’s theorem.",
              "work": "\\(z^5=(\\sqrt2)^5e^{-5i\\pi/12}=4\\sqrt2e^{19i\\pi/12}.\\)"
            }
